        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(seo): escape JSON-LD script content to prevent breakout",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`Layout.astro` embeds structured data with\n`set:html={JSON.stringify(item)}`. If any string field contains\n`</script>`, the HTML parser closes the ld+json script element early\n(classic JSON-in-script breakout).\n\n## Evidence\n\n```console\n$ node -e 'const item={name:\"</script><script>alert(1)</script>\"};\n  const bad=JSON.stringify(item);\n  const good=JSON.stringify(item).replace(/</g,\"\\\\u003c\");\n  console.log(\"bad_contains_raw_close:\", bad.includes(\"</script>\"));\n  console.log(\"good_contains_raw_close:\", good.includes(\"</script>\"));\n  console.log(\"good_json:\", good);\n  console.log(\"roundtrip:\", JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(good)));'\n\nbad_contains_raw_close: true\ngood_contains_raw_close: false\ngood_json: {\"name\":\"\\u003c/script>\\u003cscript>alert(1)\\u003c/script>\",\"n\":1}\nroundtrip: {\"name\":\"</script><script>alert(1)</script>\",\"n\":1}\n\n$ rg -n 'application/ld+json' src/layouts/Layout.astro\n79:      <script type=\"application/ld+json\" set:html={JSON.stringify(item).replace(/</g, \"\\u003c\")} />\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nEscape `<` as `\\u003c` after JSON.stringify so HTML parsers stay inside the\nscript element; JSON.parse still restores original characters.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** JSON-LD script breakout via literal </script> in stringified data\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS, Node 22+, branch fix/json-ld-script-escape\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** node escape demo; rg Layout.astro line\n- **Evidence after fix:** terminal output above (raw close gone after escape; roundtrip preserves name)\n- **Observed result after fix:** escaped payload cannot close the script tag early; data still parses\n- **What was not tested:** full astro build HTML snapshot in browser DevTools (Vercel preview blocked for forks)\n\n## Related\n\n- React/Next JSON-LD `\\u003c` guidance\n- Same-repo XSS series #140, #142, #146\n",
